{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He said</b> — The word of mercy in all of Scripture is from the heavy [binyan] [hitpa'el]." "<b>And I will show you mercy</b> — From the light [binyan] [kal], and it is not a transitive verb, in the manner of: 'my bowels came out of me,' 'they went out from me,' 'you have strengthened me, strength from me,' and this is: I seek mercy from you. And some say: like the Targum of 'loved you.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The four examples ('בני יצאוני...' etc.) are quoted very elliptically; translated hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra gives them, without reconstructing the underlying full forms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:31.088197241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}